My negotiation setup —
My BATNA (best alternative if no deal): Sign the competing pilot with Globex.
My target (what I'm aiming for): 5,000 a month
My bottom line / walk-away point: 4,200 a month

Acoustically measured speaking rate for this session: ~4.0 syllables/sec (≈ 240 syllables/min). Use this for the pace read rather than guessing from the text.

Filler watchlist (judge OVER-use of these as verbal crutches only — ignore meaningful uses, and ignore non-lexical um/uh sounds): like, you know, i mean, basically, actually, literally, sort of, kind of, kinda, sorta, you see, i guess, right?, so yeah, to be honest, at the end of the day, or whatever, and stuff, 那個, 這個, 就是, 就是說, 然後, 反正, 其實, 基本上, 怎麼講, 怎麼說, 你知道, 你知道嗎, 你懂嗎, 對不對, 對啊對啊, 這樣子, 之類的, 什麼的, 老實說, 說真的, 的部分, 的話

